Z||000004||Nashco||10-19-2001||04:09 PM||||Anniston, Alabama????  Holy crap, I live here (not from around here though), and I had no idea!  I suppose I ought to find this place, huh?  Especially seeing as I want to replace my carpet....interesting, very interesting.<P>Has anybody got carpet from ACC?  They seem to have a pretty good line, but I'm curious of the fit.  If the fit is like original or better, I would love to get one of these.<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT<p>[This message has been edited by Nashco (edited 10-19-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||LT1 Chop Top||10-19-2001||05:58 PM||||I have ACC in my Chop Top.  I think the quality is about 70% of the quality of the material of what stock is, but it LOOKS 100% better (more modern IMO). Don't remember what I paid for it, but it fits well...and seems to be standing up well.  Install was easy except removing the odd star head seatbelt bolts (used my biggest flat head).<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/87.3.jpg"> <BR>Custom floor mats and door carpet is Mr. Mikes.  Also, the carpet is MUCH darker (very black) in person.....||||reg||1
Z||000006||danny boy||10-19-2001||06:29 PM|||| they quoted me $160 when I called a few months ago.||||reg||1
Z||000007||FieroBUZZ||10-19-2001||06:47 PM||||There is a place near me in Ontario.  They quoted about $200 CDN.  Email if you want their addy or details, they don't have a website.  They should have an ad in the Canada Wide Old Car Trader, tho.<BR>Gary||||reg||1
